ve a full refund.\n8. Legal consequences of unenforceable discretionary terms. Consumer-contract terms that\nprovide for the exercise of discretion by a business without good faith are inconsistent with\nsubsection (a) and are unenforceable by the business under subsection (b). If such terms can be\nsevered from the rest of the agreement, they are replaced with gap-fillers, as described in § 10. If\nseverance or restriction of the terms cannot be accomplished by reformation or augmentation of\n99\n@§5\n"